    "origin": "model_proposed",
    "n_params": 3,
    "rationale": "Linear incumbent explains ~90% of variance (NMSE 0.0969). Residuals show negligible bias but non-trivial variance (RMSE 0.0206, bias^2/MSE=0.0098), indicating a missing structural term rather than an offset correction. The largest per-bin RMSE appears in the high-|v| region, with mild non-monotonic pattern in v-residuals. A cubic stiffness term (Duffing oscillator extension) is the canonical physical next step for a nonlinear oscillator and adds only one parameter. It is monotone in x and preserves odd symmetry, which is appropriate for a restoring force.\n\nPredicted NMSE: drop of at least 0.04 (from 0.0969 to below 0.057) if cubic stiffness is structurally relevant, or smaller if the nonlinearity is in v instead. Risk: if the true nonlinearity is quadratic damping or v^2-based, NMSE may not improve much. That would redirect the next attempt to a v|v| or v^2 term.\n\nThis is an incremental structural extension based on physical priors and residual diagnostics; it is not a claim that the oscillator is necessarily Duffing or that training-fit improvement implies held-out improvement.",
